359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (Large Language Models \(LLMs\) are fundamentally prediction engines, not knowledge bases. They generate text by predicting the most statistically likely next word based on patterns learned from training data. They do not understand truth, they predict plausibility. When the model encounters a gap in its training data or faces an ambiguous query, the mathematics of its softmax function force it to guess the most plausible-sounding continuation, bridging gaps in logic with seamless fiction.For computer science engineers, the mandate is clear: we can no longer treat these hallucinations as traditional software "bugs" that can be patched. Because this stochastic behaviour is mathematically inevitable, absolute reliability must be engineered through external architectural oversight.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 107 0 R
/T (Engineering Reliability:)
/E (Engineering Reliability:)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 107 0 R
/T (Reflection and Hierarchical Verification)
/E (Reflection and Hierarchical Verification)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (Contemporary research has moved decisively away from single-pass inference towards multi-layered verification architectures. Instead of relying on a single, flawed generative pass, we deploy both internal and external auditing mechanisms to force the model to reason accurately.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 107 0 R
/T (Intrinsic Reflection \(Self-Correction\))
/E (Intrinsic Reflection \(Self-Correction\))
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (The first line of defence is intrinsic reflection. Instead of outputting its initial statistical prediction, the model is forced into an iterative self-critique loop. It drafts a response in a hidden scratchpad, and a secondary system prompt instructs the model to critique its own logic checking for contradictions and unsupported claims before delivering the final output.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
