448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (Contemporary research has moved decisively away from single-pass inference towards multi-layered verification architectures. Instead of relying on a single, flawed generative pass, we deploy both internal and external auditing mechanisms to force the model to reason accurately.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 111 0 R
/T (Intrinsic Reflection \(Self-Correction\))
/E (Intrinsic Reflection \(Self-Correction\))
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (The first line of defence is intrinsic reflection. Instead of outputting its initial statistical prediction, the model is forced into an iterative self-critique loop. It drafts a response in a hidden scratchpad, and a secondary system prompt instructs the model to critique its own logic checking for contradictions and unsupported claims before delivering the final output.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
