510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (This is the 21st century and it is the era of AI, from studies to business and offices  AI is everywhere, people are undoubtedly benefiting a lot from this because this complex system has made their lives very much easier, but think about existence of AI two centuries ago,, there was no AI, the 19th century was of steam engines, industrial revolutions and empires. What if these two eras collide? I mean what if AI existed in the late 19s century)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
511 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Today AI is transforming civilizations, transforming our way of living. Think about education, healthcare , robotics, transportation , entertainment ,cybersecurity , and what not?. AI has made everything easier. But in 19th century or even before that why was AI not invented?. actually AI heavily depends on modern computation, huge amounts of data and algorithms. The 19th century lacked modern computers , it was not the lack of data but the storage was unavailable, data was only stored in pen and paper. And the level of algorithms needed to build AI was also not available at that time. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Yet imagining a scenario where AI existed in 19th century reveals both the power and limitation of AI. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (AI is largely based on data and  algorithms. The main part on which AI heavily depends is machine learning. Developers have to train the computer through huge amounts of data called datasets, they train their programs in such a way that they can easily recognise patterns and tackle complex problems. The algorithm works through various layers called neural networks. These neural networks extract patterns from examples in training datasets. They search for patterns in multiple steps. Once a programme has been trained on a dataset, it can then encounter new scenarios and also can make predictions. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E ( All these happen after the programme is trained by various examples by the dataset.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Now if we imagine these things in the 19th century, this sounds absurd, maybe the words did not exist like networks or datasets. But if we think deeply a non developed AI system could have existed because at that time huge amounts of data were not stored there but some data were still there which could have been used to predict outcome. Think of it like a baby, his parents teach him when to do what,, and once after some years the kid takes decisions of his own,, this is his own intelligence. A similar thing happens in AI but artificially.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (So why not in the 19th century?.it could have  existed but like a primitive child because AI needs many things which were not there in the past,, like no GPUs, no transistors , very limited storage and above all no internet, the machines were mostly mechanical, computation was still there in that time but at a very primary level. One example is analytical engine invented by Charles Babbage in 1837. So as said previously, AI could have existed like a primitive child, although modern AI would be impossible , primitive mechanical intelligence or rule based systems might still have emerged.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [21]
>>
