/Title (However, a model cannot always detect its own blind spots. When intrinsic reflection fails, the state-of-the-art relies on extrinsic hierarchical verification, known as the Proposer-Verifier-Synthesiser pattern. This mirrors dual-process theory in cognitive psychology by dividing tasks into intuitive generation and analytical reasoning.)
